.vs/

# VAPT "Information Disclosure": runtime logs and build-output *.dll.config files can contain
# stack traces, IPs, usernames, and (bin/*.dll.config specifically) plaintext DB credentials copied
# in by the build - none of that belongs in source control.
CPSC(Tata)/Logs/*.txt
CPSC(Tata)/bin/
CPSC(Tata)/obj/

# NuGet-restored packages: never intentionally tracked (confirmed via git ls-files before adding
# this line), but packages.config-style restore extracts binaries straight into this folder, and
# it was never excluded here - so it showed up as 80+ pending "changes" the first time someone
# actually looked at Git Changes with a fully-restored packages/ present. These are restorable
# from packages.config, not source - they don't belong in git.
/packages/
